# nvn/memory: a memory-pressure response that trims caches at the next submission (system pressure source, app request, headroom watermark); DM_MEM_PRESSURE, DM_MEM_TRIM, DM_MEM_HEADROOM
#
# Source:    https://github.com/mianmuhammadse/nxnative  branch no-bc, commits 2ad4c0d4 ("Memory-pressure response: trims caches on a memory warning, a system memory-pressure event or low
#            headroom (iOS)") and 69e26193 ("Use the texture registry unfair lock during pressure trim")
# Author:    Mian Muhammad (the commits' author)
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE; the fork keeps it). The attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# Why: iOS stops an app at its footprint limit (about 3 GB on a 6 GB iPhone 15, the fork measured), usually with no warning it can act on; the no-BC iPhones are the 4-6 GB ones.
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m; test t_mem_trim):
#   Requests (they only set a tier): the system memory-pressure source mtl_init_once already had (warn = tier 1, critical = tier 2; it still trims the render-target heaps at once),
#   mtl_mem_pressure_request(tier, reason) for the app (exported: the app's memory warning can call it with reason 3), and a watermark on os_proc_available_memory() every 30 game frames
#   (mtl_mem_pressure_tick from mtl_set_frame): tier 1 under 300 MB of headroom, tier 2 under 150 MB, asked again at most every 300 frames unless the tier rises.
#   The trim, at the next mtl_sub_begin (submit thread, nothing encoded yet): the view cache (g_vc) emptied, rh_trim, one GPU wait then defer_drain, the staging slots' blocks of batches
#   not in flight dropped (made again by the next upload), malloc_zone_pressure_relief. One line: "memory pressure: tier N (reason, frame), headroom, footprint, GPU allocated before ->
#   after: ...". Nothing runs while the headroom is fine (one os_proc_available_memory call every 30 frames).
# Adapted: the fork's trim cuts upstream's ghost table and drops unreferenced shared textures and re-upload spares; this tree keeps those in nvn_owner.m with other lifetimes (a spare is
#   reused by a re-upload on another thread, under other locks), so they are NOT trimmed here. The fork also moved later deferred releases forward after its GPU wait: not here (an upload
#   batch committed outside a submission may still hold them). Its UIApplicationDidReceiveMemoryWarning hook is in dm/ios (not our app's front end): the app may call
#   mtl_mem_pressure_request(1, 3) itself. Its hle_nvn.c frame hook is replaced by mtl_set_frame (same thread as the trim, no new symbol between files).
# Defaults: on. DM_MEM_PRESSURE=0: requests ignored, no trim (the system source's render-target heap trim stays, as before). Test switches: DM_MEM_TRIM=<frame>:<tier>[,...],
#   DM_MEM_HEADROOM=<MB> (stands in for os_proc_available_memory, -1 = unknown on a Mac).
# On a GPU with BC: the same (this is not a no-BC feature), and nothing runs unless a request comes.
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad).
# Tests (M1 Pro): t_mem_trim (new; make check_t_mem_trim runs it and "off") 18/0 + 7/0. NOT run on a device: a real system pressure event or watermark on an iPhone is not verified.

